{
  "_what": "The formulas a workflow step with variants runs on (tools/write-a-job-done-in-several-steps-have/read-data/variants.mjs compiles such a step into a parallel loop over its variants, a compare step and the rows each run keeps in variant_results). Each formula is text, compiled by this engine (compileText) into `binding`, which the workflow engine evaluates inside a `return` step with the same shared evaluator. A formula reads only its `names`; the step compiler binds each name to a value of the run (a step's output, or a literal), so no run value is named here. Inside a lambda every value starts from the lambda's own item (a.runs, never a name with a lambda value applied to it): the workflow engine works out a name's own value before the item exists, so a name may stand inside a lambda only as it is, or as an argument. `binding` is made from `text` by `node tools/write-a-job-done-in-several-steps-have/read-data/compile-variant-formulas.mjs`; test/variants.test.mjs fails when the two differ.",
